WEBVTT

00:00:01.710 --> 00:00:02.537
Hi, I'm Jackstay!

00:00:02.537 --> 00:00:06.120
This engine runs a huge model on a Mac that cannot hold it.

00:00:10.558 --> 00:00:13.966
Most of the model is experts, and a token needs only a few.

00:00:13.966 --> 00:00:16.849
The busy ones stay in a pool of slots, and the

00:00:16.849 --> 00:00:17.897
rest wait on disk.

00:00:20.967 --> 00:00:24.170
Each layer, the router picks ten of five hundred twelve experts and

00:00:24.170 --> 00:00:25.771
looks for each in the pool.

00:00:26.191 --> 00:00:29.368
An expert already in a slot goes straight to the graphics chip,

00:00:29.368 --> 00:00:30.957
which gathers it by slot number.

00:00:31.377 --> 00:00:34.790
A missing one is read from disk into a slot, about three

00:00:34.790 --> 00:00:36.496
megabytes, with no cache in between.

00:00:36.916 --> 00:00:40.165
A forecast runs the router of a later layer early, so some

00:00:40.165 --> 00:00:42.060
reads finish before they are asked for.

00:00:43.608 --> 00:00:46.771
The pool is shared by every layer, and one simple scan

00:00:46.771 --> 00:00:47.921
chooses what to evict.

00:00:48.341 --> 00:00:50.412
A hit marks the slot as recently used.

00:00:51.272 --> 00:00:53.033
A miss sweeps a hand around the pool.

00:00:54.204 --> 00:00:56.343
It skips the slots this layer is still using.

00:00:57.135 --> 00:01:00.006
The first unmarked slot is the one that gets replaced.

00:01:01.508 --> 00:01:04.967
In the project's own runs, the pool already held the expert eighty

00:01:04.967 --> 00:01:06.985
to ninety six percent of the time.

00:01:09.300 --> 00:01:12.725
With an empty cache the disk would have to deliver almost

00:01:12.725 --> 00:01:13.970
thirty gigabytes a second.

00:01:13.970 --> 00:01:15.527
It tops out near seventeen.

00:01:17.142 --> 00:01:19.027
So the speed is a caching problem.

00:01:19.027 --> 00:01:22.796
Most lookups hit, and the disk wait is a minor part of each token.

00:01:25.608 --> 00:01:28.664
Experts on disk, a shared pool in memory, and a forecast

00:01:28.664 --> 00:01:29.775
to hide the reads.

00:01:30.208 --> 00:01:32.308
Every source is in the full article.

00:01:32.308 --> 00:01:32.908
I'm Jackstay.

00:01:32.908 --> 00:01:33.209
Bye!
